Sat Oct 17 05:01:25 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- version 1.23.3b-0
- Fix install failure: soname-exclude zen's OWN bundled NSS/NSPr stack
  (libnss3/nssutil3/ssl3/smime3/nspr4/plc4/plds4) from auto-Requires.
  libxul.so imports versioned NSS symbols up to NSSUTIL_3.130/NSS_3.126
  that the system mozilla-nss does not provide, so the 1.23.3b build
  emitted an unresolvable "nothing provides
  libnssutil3.so(NSSUTIL_3.130)(64bit)" and every zypper install broke.
  zen resolves these from its bundled copies via $ORIGIN, same rationale
  as the already-excluded moz* libs; libnssckbi.so still comes from the
  system (mozilla-nss-certs Requires + symlink). Verified: 1.23.3b RPM
  install failed before, installs clean after in a fresh TW container.
- Define PACKAGER_ADDR in update.sh (was referenced but unset, which wrote
  an empty .changes heading).

